{
  "id": "Compound::DB00216 - Gene::3351",
  "verbalization": "Eletriptan is linked to Htr1b through a series of molecular interactions that involve serotonin receptor agonism. The evidence suggests that Eletriptan, as part of the serotonin 1b and 1d receptor agonist family, binds to Rizatriptan, which in turn interacts with Htr1b. This pathway is supported by the lowest common ancestor relationship between Eletriptan and Rizatriptan, both of which share a common connection to indoles and serotonin agonists. The presence of Htr1e as a participant in serotonin binding further reinforces the involvement of Htr1b in the signaling cascade. The integration of these relationships highlights a potential mechanism where Eletriptan modulates Htr1b through serotonin receptor activation, suggesting a role in the regulation of serotonin signaling and possibly in the pathophysiology of related conditions.",
